#
# An abseil flagfile, consumed as `verible-verilog-format --flagfile=...`. It is
# checked in so that the dev shell, the CI check and any editor integration cannot
# disagree about what "formatted" means — the same argument .clang-format makes for
# the C++ in ddd-gui/.
#
# Do not point this at fpga/src/IPfifo.v, IPfifo_bb.v, IPpllGenerator.v or
# IPpllGenerator_bb.v. Those are MegaWizard output treated as source of truth and
# AGENTS.md section 3 says not to reformat them; tests/run-format.sh names the files
# it touches rather than globbing, for exactly that reason.

# Four spaces, matching .editorconfig's [*.{v,sv,svh,vh}] indent_size = 4 and the C,
# C++, Python and shell settings across the rest of the tree. This is a deliberate
# deviation from lowRISC's two — a tree-wide indent convention is worth more than
# agreement with an external document on a point that carries no meaning.
--indentation_spaces=4

# The sources already fit inside 100 columns, so a limit tighter than
# .editorconfig's max_line_length = 120 costs nothing and is worth keeping.
--column_limit=100

# Every alignment mode is set explicitly rather than left at Verible's default of
# `infer`. `infer` guesses the intent from how the file is already laid out, which
# makes the output depend on its own input — the non-determinism this file exists to
# remove. The formatter owns column alignment outright.
#
# The accepted cost: adding one long signal name re-aligns its neighbouring group, so
# an occasional diff touches lines the author did not edit.
--assignment_statement_alignment=align
--case_items_alignment=align
--class_member_variable_alignment=align
--distribution_items_alignment=align
--enum_assignment_statement_alignment=align
--formal_parameters_alignment=align
--module_net_variable_alignment=align
--named_parameter_alignment=align
--named_port_alignment=align
--port_declarations_alignment=align
--struct_union_members_alignment=align

# Re-formatting formatted output must be a no-op. On by default; written down because
# a non-convergent formatter would make the CI check flap.
--verify_convergence=true
